        <mxCell id="visitor" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Public visitor&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Anonymous&lt;/span&gt;" style="shape=umlActor;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;html=1;outlineConnect=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#1c1c1c;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1c1c1c;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="66" y="220" width="44" height="52" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pipe" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Delivery pipeline&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Site + origin lock.&lt;br&gt;Function ZipDeploy&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9a9aa8;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=10;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="410" width="140" height="90" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="publisher" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Publisher&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Entra group&lt;/span&gt;" style="shape=umlActor;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;html=1;outlineConnect=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#1c1c1c;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1c1c1c;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="66" y="640" width="44" height="52" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="entra" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Microsoft Entra ID&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Sign-in, roles&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9a9aa8;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=10;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="830" width="140" height="90" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notify" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Notification channels&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Email, webhooks&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9a9aa8;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=10;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1560" y="890" width="200" height="100" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c1" parent="1" value="HTTPS" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" source="visitor" target="fd"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c2" parent="1" value="Protects" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;" edge="1" source="waf" target="fd"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c3" parent="1" value="/*" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" source="fd" target="swa"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c4" parent="1" value="/api/* via Private Link" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.9;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.15;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" source="fd" target="func"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c5" parent="1" value="VNet integration" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" source="func" target="snet"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c6" parent="1" value="Managed identity" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" source="func" target="pe"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c7" parent="1" value="Private link" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" source="pe" target="store"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c8" parent="1" value="Resolves names" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;" edge="1" source="pe" target="dnsz"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c9" parent="1" value="Deploys site" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;" edge="1" source="pipe" target="swa"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c10" parent="1" value="Uploads PDFs" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" source="publisher" target="store"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c11" parent="1" value="Signs in" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;" edge="1" source="publisher" target="entra"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c12" parent="1" value="Test results" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" source="ai" target="alerts"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c13" parent="1" value="Stores telemetry" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;" edge="1" source="law" target="ai"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c14" parent="1" value="Fires" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" source="alerts" target="ag"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c15" parent="1" value="Email, webhook" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#3c3c3c;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" source="ag" target="notify"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-1" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Request and publishing paths: what they do and why&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Website path:&lt;/b&gt; Front Door ends TLS, redirects HTTP to HTTPS, applies the WAF and routes /* to the Static Web App. The Static Web App accepts only AzureFrontDoor.Backend traffic that carries this profile&amp;apos;s X-Azure-FDID header and a listed forwarded host, so the default azurestaticapps.net address cannot bypass the WAF.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;API path:&lt;/b&gt; /api/* goes to the Function App through a Private Link connection that Front Door requests and the deploy script approves. The Function has public network access disabled, so Front Door is the only way in.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read path:&lt;/b&gt; The Function signs in with its system-assigned identity (Storage Blob Data Reader), lists or streams blobs over the private endpoint, keeps only .pdf blobs with approved=true and answers 404 for missing and unapproved alike.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Publish path:&lt;/b&gt; Publishers sign in with Entra ID (Storage Blob Data Contributor) and upload PDFs with approved=true over the storage public endpoint. No network path and no code release are needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;No caching:&lt;/b&gt; /api/* has no cache rule and responses are no-store, so a publication or withdrawal shows at once.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Checks:&lt;/b&gt; Standard web tests open / and /api/documents every 5 minutes from 3 locations and check the certificate. Alerts cover Front Door 5xx and origin health, and Function 5xx.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Does not prove:&lt;/b&gt; that a document is correct or approved by the business (approved=true is a process control), that the Function code is deployed, or that DNS and certificates for custom domains are valid.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1c1c1c;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="1190" width="840" height="392" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-2" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;The same story in plain language&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;What happens&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;â€¢ A visitor opens the website. A security gate in front of it checks the request and shows the page&lt;br&gt;â€¢ The page asks for the list of documents. That request goes to a private service that nobody can reach directly&lt;br&gt;â€¢ The private service reads the documents from locked storage and shows only the ones marked approved&lt;br&gt;â€¢ A publisher adds or removes documents without changing any code&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why we do it this way&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;â€¢ The public only ever meets the security gate, never the storage or the service behind it&lt;br&gt;â€¢ The service has its own identity, so there are no passwords or keys in the code&lt;br&gt;â€¢ Tests check the site and the document list every 5 minutes and alert the team when they fail&lt;br&gt;â€¢ The same shape in every environment means testing in dev tells us what production will do&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1c1c1c;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="920" y="1190" width="840" height="216" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-3" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;What to keep in mind&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Origin lock is a pipeline step:&lt;/b&gt; the Static Web App accepts only this Front Door once the site pipeline writes staticwebapp.config.json from SWA_CONFIG_JSON. The Front Door ID changes if Front Door is recreated.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Private Link is approved by script:&lt;/b&gt; the connection is created Pending. Until deploy.sh approves it, /api/* fails.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Function deployment needs a private path:&lt;/b&gt; its package is deployed over its private endpoint, so the deploy job must run on an agent inside the network.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Custom domains:&lt;/b&gt; each needs a DNS validation record before its managed certificate is issued, and certificate renewal depends on the DNS provider.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Weakest link:&lt;/b&gt; storage keeps shared-key access on for the Function host and accepts authenticated requests from any network. Treat the account keys as secrets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Access:&lt;/b&gt; publishers are Entra groups, viewers and operators get Reader and Monitoring Contributor on the resource group.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cost:&lt;/b&gt; about $553 a month fixed in dev and qa, about $707 in uat and prod (retail prices, West Europe, 2026-10-30). Front Door Premium is $330 of that and one EP1 instance is about $154. Traffic is extra. Budgets: 600 in dev and qa, 800 in uat, 900 in prod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Status:&lt;/b&gt; nothing has been built or deployed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1c1c1c;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="1612" width="840" height="392" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-4" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Why pick this design, and its trade-offs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Front Door Premium in every environment, not Standard in dev:&lt;/b&gt; Private Link origins and managed WAF rules need Premium, and one shape everywhere means dev tests what prod runs. Trade-off: $330 a month even in dev.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Private Link to the Function, not a public API with restrictions:&lt;/b&gt; the API cannot be called except through the WAF. Trade-off: the connection must be approved and deployments need a private network path.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Elastic Premium EP1, not Consumption:&lt;/b&gt; VNet integration with private endpoints and a warm instance, so no cold start. Trade-off: about $154 a month per instance with no traffic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;One storage account, not two:&lt;/b&gt; the Function host and the documents share an account, matching the reviewed design and keeping publishing simple. Trade-off: shared-key access stays on and the endpoint is open to authenticated requests from any network; the hardened option is two accounts with a private publishing path.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Managed identity, not keys or SAS:&lt;/b&gt; a compromised API cannot write or delete documents. Trade-off: the Reader role is account-wide, not per container.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zone redundancy on in uat and prod:&lt;/b&gt; a zone failure should not take the API offline. Trade-off: two EP1 instances double the compute cost and the setting is fixed at creation. Front Door and Static Web Apps are global, so they have no zone setting.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Deployment stack per environment, not Terraform state:&lt;/b&gt; removes what you remove from the template with nothing to bootstrap. Trade-off: the stack is the only record and there is no plan file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1c1c1c;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="920" y="1612" width="840" height="408" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
